oro without his permission it's  pretty clear already that enma will be  the key to the victory in this fight but  before that zorro has to figure out how  to actually use it to its full potential  king's comments are hilarious too as he  asks zoro trouble in paradise it is  strange to see a source swordsman  quarreling with his sword and king will  definitely bring that up more in this  chapter but a common theme we're seeing  in one piece recently is that the best  swords are more like partners to the  swordsmen rather than just dead tools  and although in the short term king's  blade seems much simpler to use and more  effective enma's difficulty of use will  no doubt correlate with greater  potential down the line for now though  zoro stabs king king has the best  reaction ever saying ah a direct hit  not worried at all then he appears to  explode and we jump to sanji really it's  not so much about sanji's fight here as  it's about giving us more information  about zorro and king queen confirms that  king is in fact the surviving lunarian  he tells us they were all supposed to be  eradicated he comments that those  monsters as he calls them could thrive  in any inhospitable environment the  world threw at them people like that may  even be able to survive on the moon as  their name suggests queen even says they  were considered gods in the past and i'm  glad sanji actually asked the question  we're probably all wondering how come  they're so op and yet they got  eradicated but queen says as if oda  himself is teasing us through queen  that's something you'll have to find out  for yourself that's yet another thing  i'm super curious about but for now  within that story there is a suggestion  that king can obviously be defeated by  zorro if almost all of the godlike  people were wiped out if i had to guess  i'd assume that it was the world  government in a coordinated effort and  perhaps with a surprise attack that  wiped them out but we shall see whoever  did it 