ext he  reaches out for wado ichimonji the sword  he got from kuina thinking it's a relief  it didn't fall off the island we get a  flashback to way back near the beginning  of the series when zoro begged kuina's  father for her sword and promises that  he'll get strong enough that his name  reaches up to the heavens and that he'll  become the greatest swordsman for  himself and for her i've been saying  this is and is going to continue to be a  heavily zoro focused arc and having this  flashback back to his origin only  solidifies that i also like the mention  of reaching up to the heavens since it's  a nice contrast with enma named after  the god of the underworld pretty much at  the end of the series you know zoro's  going to be saying we started from the  bottom that we hear we then get back to  zorro speaking to swordsmith tenguyama  hitetsu in the past and the latter  telling him it must be fate that zorro  gets enma because enma and wado  ichimonji were forged by the same man  the master swordsmith shimotsuki  kozaburo and yes he just said the title  of the chapter zorro finally starts  connecting the dots and thinking about  how a sword from wano ended up in the  east blue king continues the attack  onslaught and zoro is clearly on the  defensive as the flashbacks continue the  tsunachi convo with momo is brought up  when zoro said he heard it from an old  geezer even though he never used it  himself he never learned the geezer's  name which is pretty hilarious but he  sat by the shore a lot he only found out  this geezer was queen as grandpa after  he died he puts that back together with  hitetsu telling him that kozaburro left  the country illegally over 50 years ago  then we get a flashback all the way back  to when zoro was a kid brand new stuff  and i gotta say i've been waiting  forever for this 13 years ago in  shimotsuki village the geezer tells zoro  that tsunachi is a battle cry that gives  one courage but hilariously zoro says he  won't use it since it sounds weird he's  such a classic annoying kid here and  it's hilarious to see he asks the geezer  if he was a samurai and the geezer  responds that zoro should be quiet or  the marines will come for him they  exchange insults but the geezer whose  look is just amazing i must say takes  note of zorro's energy and how hard he  trains zoro at one point tells the  geezer he lost to kuina so he needs to  train non-stop not just in the dojo the  geezer gives him two real swords even  though zoro has no money so there we  have yet another epic and rude old dude  with a heart of gold in one piece the  geezer goes on to imply that these  swords aren't as special as his old ones  and proceeds to educate us about swords  like we've been saying each blade is  like a person with a unique disposition  not just dead tools a swordsman is one  who tames the sword's wild nature and  bends it to their will and here we get a  cool moment where zoro's told it's a  joke when people say swords are cursed  it's just how name blades are it's  praise rather than anything else they  fulfill their purpose of taking life and  this explains why zoro was so undaunted  by the fact that his sword was set to be  cursed it's a really nice touch and i'm  glad we got it in this chapter klosaburo  tells zorro he crafted his magnum opus  aka his masterpiece when he was still  young the temperament of the sword was  something else it would give chills to  those holding it he named it after the  lord of the underworld and zorro finally  realizes that that sword is the sword in  front of him aka enma this backstory  mid-fight was masterfully done i love  the backstory itself but it was also  perfect for adding significance to this  fight and to enma specifically the  implication is the more problematic the  sword like enma the better it is when  one can finally sync up with it and that  is the task set before zorro gotta also  say i absolutely love this old dude  kozaburo is a boss finally zoro realizes  that his village being called shimotsuki  doesn't seem like a coincidence anymore  he finally says that that old geezer was  a samurai wano specifically the  swordsmith shimotsuki kozaburo and as he  says this all i can think is imagine how  hilarious it would be if zoro had  sherlock holmes job but lastly he  remembers being told that named blades  stay vigilant patiently waiting to find  a swordsman worthy of them and that a  sword chooses its wielder and zoro  realizes that enma is just testing him  it's not resisting him or acting out of  malice zorro just hasn't been measuring  up to its standards and he is odd that  odin was easily able to wield enma with  this much haki pouring out of him love  the look of the black and enma 2 in this  panel the implication is that zoro once  mastering anima will be near odin level  or at least a lot closer to it which is  hype since we know what odin did to  kaido albeit to a younger kaido at the  very least i think it's safe to say  it'll be enough to beat king then as  underlings tried to rush zorro his  conqueror's haki causes them to faint  always cool seeing zoro use conquerors  haki zoro remarks that he can only  appease enma with all of his hockey and  that could kill him but as we know  zoro's never been one to shy away from  situations that could kill him in fact  he goes through them and says nothing  happened i really like this aspect it  wasn't about him needing to tame enma  per se but about enma forcing him to  step up and go beyond what he thought  would be possible as we see zoro all his  blades are burning overflowing with haki  and king sees that he has kingly  ambitions as well which is pretty much a  way of saying he's got conquerors haki  and just to top off this beautiful  chapter my favorite in a while zoro  thinks of his meeting with luffy way  back then luffy said the future king of  the pirates would settle for nothing  less than the world's greatest swordsman  zorro tells king i guess you're right  after all i made promises to my captain  and my oldest friend thus were reminded  of what makes zorro tick the promise he  made to queena to luffy and his own  desire to be the best swordsman in the  world we're told zoro is surpassing  limits which is hype since it is pretty  much confirming that zorro just became  and is becoming the strongest he's ever  been this might be my favorite zorro  focus chapter yet but let me know if  there's one you prefer more obviously  zorro has had many great moments but the  way they tied up his backstory here and  had him reaffirm his goal with the new  power up it's just too good i won't even  ask you who was mvp here because it's  obviously zorro although i would also  accept enma as an answer since swords  are practically living characters at  this point and that is it for as i said  one of my favorite chapters in a while i  loved it let me know what you thought  about it and what you're expecting to  see happening next will zorro crush king  suddenly or will we get more back and  forth moments as zoro's power continues  to increase if you did enjoy this review  and want to keep them coming you know  what to do channel the pirate king  within and smash that like button with  no mercy as we all know smashing that  like button is pirating energy and  passing is orochi energy so choose  wisely if you haven't make this the  video subscribe this is crucial hit that  notification bell to turn on all  notifications or you will miss future  one-piece videos and updates that's just  the way it works and while you wait for  the next chapter to drop feel free to  check out my huge and growing one piece  playlist that includes videos on all  yonko admirals supernova and much more  link to that is in the description and  until next time see ya space cowboys  [Music]  so  [Music]  you

